{
  "dom_id": "questionContainer",
  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following conditional probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)={\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x, & \\,0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(X<Y\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{\\pi }{3}).$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n$$\nP(X\\in A\\,|\\,Y=y)={\\int }_{A}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ is the conditional probability density function of $X$ given $Y=y.$ \n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<Y\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =P(X<\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y=\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x]_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
